 ### Chamfer Distance with Color
-Extends CD to include color fidelity. It computes a weighted sum of geometric distance and color distance (L2 norm of RGB differences between nearest neighbors). The loss is $\alpha \cdot \text{mean}(\text{geo}) + (1-\alpha) \cdot \text{mean}(\text{color})$, with $\alpha=0.5$ by default [S17, unofficial].
