 ## Background
 
-Chamfer Distance originated as a metric for comparing point sets and has become a standard evaluation tool in 3D computer vision, particularly for neural rendering and implicit surface reconstruction. It is widely used in conjunction with F-Score to provide a comprehensive view of geometric accuracy [S1, unofficial][S10]. The metric is frequently reported in papers dealing with mesh reconstruction methods like Self-Supervised Dual Contouring [S2, S4]. It is also used in Gaussian Splatting optimization for mesh refinement [S16, unofficial].
